//? Title: Timsort: actual natural runs, extension and stable merge stacks
//? Subtitle: Actual canonical histories, retained original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Adaptive sorting detects order already present in the input, extends short runs,
and merges adjacent runs stably. Actual sorting events and the shared native
raw-run detector distinguish the original input profile from the runs consumed
after extension.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and mathematical scope

Nondecreasing runs retain equal-key order; only strictly descending runs are
reversed. Binary insertion uses an upper bound for equal keys, and merges prefer
the earlier left run on ties. Minrun is computed by shifting until below64 and
retaining discarded low bits. Merge-collapse checks include both the top-three
and next-deeper inequalities; this repairs the old top-three-only policy.
Galloping is omitted. The standard run-stack strategy gives adaptive stable O(n
log n) worst-case comparison behavior and a linear scan on already ordered
input. Raw input run count is not the count of runs consumed after short-run
extension.

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native concept diagram read the same producing execution. Every
block below is a complete editable C++ program.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/timsort_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    std::vector<int> keys(64);
    std::iota(keys.begin(), keys.begin() + 32, 32);
    std::iota(keys.begin() + 32, keys.end(), 0);
    auto r = a::timsort_trace(keys);
    std::print("| actual action | base | left length | right length | actual stack lengths | complete " "actual keys |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &s : r.steps)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | `{}` | `{}` |\n", s.action, s.base,
                   s.left_length, s.right_length, s.stack_lengths,
                   std::vector<int>(s.after.begin(),
                                    s.after.begin() + std::min<std::size_t>(
                                    8, s.after.size())));
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Actual two ascending32-key runs");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0}, std::format("Actual minrun {}", r.minrun));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual merges; {} runs", r.merges,
                                     r.natural_runs));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/timsort_tiny.svg");
}
```
