> API and interpretation

Copyable strict-weak-order keys are supported; nonfinite built-in floating
values reject. The in-place compatibility sort replaces caller data only on
success. Full int index/key geometry and actual comparisons/assignments/history
policies are checked. The shared raw-run detector is used by both input
profiling and the actual sort, and only producer events claim actual sorting
states.

Reusable producers, fixtures and histories live in the canonical C++ library.
Captured records own their values and do not come from a separate report replay.
Selected counters and record/scalar policies are specified at their API
boundaries; they are not peak-byte or wall-time budgets. Synthetic structural
inputs are controlled fixtures for these mechanisms.

> References

- [Peters, CPython listsort design and merge-stack policy|https://github.com/python/cpython/blob/v3.10.0/Objects/listsort.txt]

